Now I have sufficient evidence for a thorough assessment. Let me synthesize my findings.

**Verification Summary:**
- DEGAP RAMS 54.2 / WikiEvents 67.1 Arg-C F1: ✅ **CONFIRMED** (fetched from arXiv HTML)
- LtGaE arXiv:2603.02909, AAAI 2026: ✅ **CONFIRMED** (AAAI OJS page exists)
- Gatto et al. arXiv:2403.03304 at ACL 2025 Long: ✅ **CONFIRMED** (ACL Anthology 2025.acl-long.1221)
- GuideX at ACL Findings 2025: ✅ **CONFIRMED** (ACL Anthology 2025.findings-acl.1245)
- ASEE arXiv:2505.08690 at EMNLP Findings 2025: ✅ **CONFIRMED** (ACL Anthology 2025.findings-emnlp.419)
- XGrammar <40μs/token claim: ✅ **CONFIRMED** (default backend for vLLM/SGLang/TensorRT-LLM as of March 2026)
- No directly competing concurrent work on hard grammar constraint comparison for synthetic EAE training data: ✅ **CONFIRMED**
- **Newly found**: FineCSDA (NLPCC 2024) addresses rare argument roles in document-level EAE via LLM augmentation — **NOT cited in proposal**, but no formal grammar constraints used

